WEBVTT

00:00:21.320 --> 00:00:24.140
In other news, a virus has been detected.

00:00:24.140 --> 00:00:30.000
The WHO has declared this virus to be one of the most dangerous—

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:34.400
Sources within the Japanese government have accepted the offer from the U.S. government

00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:36.010
for an emergency supply of vaccines—

00:00:36.050 --> 00:00:40.440
This virus's incubation time ranges from 30 to 50 days.

00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:44.020
Priority has been placed on procuring vaccines for the 2,000 citizens under quarant—

00:00:44.020 --> 00:00:47.300
Telephone service is mostly unavailable in Hinamizawa,

00:00:47.300 --> 00:00:49.520
preventing the prefectural disaster
management department from evalua—

00:00:49.520 --> 00:00:54.030
Furthermore, all highways leading to
quarantined areas have been shut down,

00:00:54.030 --> 00:00:59.040
<i>and all railway lines will be
avoiding the quarantined areas.</i>

00:00:54.800 --> 00:00:57.940
What's got everyone so riled up so early?

00:00:57.940 --> 00:01:01.220
This is the Emergency Response Headquarters.

00:01:01.220 --> 00:01:03.390
Beginning at noon today,

00:01:03.390 --> 00:01:08.140
there will be a mass medical
examination at Hinamizawa School.

00:01:08.140 --> 00:01:13.300
Please follow the instructions of your local representatives and gather there.

00:01:11.940 --> 00:01:13.300
This is awful!

00:01:13.770 --> 00:01:16.990
They found a killer virus or something.

00:01:16.990 --> 00:01:19.250
What terrible timing.

00:01:19.250 --> 00:01:22.230
I have to go to Osaka tomorrow...

00:01:22.230 --> 00:01:24.090
Huh, a virus?

00:01:24.090 --> 00:01:25.630
What are we going to do?

00:01:25.630 --> 00:01:28.240
There was supposed to be a sale at Okinomiya today,

00:01:28.240 --> 00:01:30.260
so I've got nothing in the fridge.

00:01:30.260 --> 00:01:32.130
And the water's been turned off too!

00:01:32.130 --> 00:01:33.940
Just what is going on here?

00:01:33.320 --> 00:01:36.160
A few weeks after being infected,

00:01:36.160 --> 00:01:41.330
infected persons will begin exhibiting the following symptoms, which can lead to death in a week—

00:01:45.410 --> 00:01:48.990
Hinamizawa and other areas
specified by the prefectural governor

00:01:48.990 --> 00:01:50.750
have been placed under quarantine.

00:01:51.420 --> 00:01:57.790
Until the safety of the quarantined area can be determined, you may not leave this district.

00:01:57.790 --> 00:02:03.140
Those who do not abide by this decree will be punished in accordance with national law.

00:02:03.140 --> 00:02:07.560
Please return to your homes and remain calm.

00:02:08.110 --> 00:02:10.050
We repeat.

00:02:10.050 --> 00:02:13.080
This is the Ground Self-Defense Force.

00:02:13.080 --> 00:02:15.680
As of 4 AM this morning,

00:02:15.680 --> 00:02:19.440
Hinamizawa and other areas
specified by the prefectural governor

00:02:19.440 --> 00:02:21.710
have been placed under quarantine.

00:02:21.710 --> 00:02:27.410
Until the safety of the quarantined area can be determined, you may not leave this district.

00:02:22.030 --> 00:02:25.240
Hinamizawa is under quarantine?

00:02:28.220 --> 00:02:33.420
Those who do not abide by this decree will be punished in accordance with national law.

00:02:31.920 --> 00:02:33.420
The phones aren't working either?

00:02:33.420 --> 00:02:37.960
Please return to your homes and remain calm.

00:02:34.360 --> 00:02:36.260
Keiichi, you do the second floor.

00:02:36.260 --> 00:02:39.140
We're going to seal up the
windows tight with packing tape.

00:02:39.010 --> 00:02:40.850
We repeat.

00:02:39.140 --> 00:02:40.990
I'll do the first floor.

00:02:40.850 --> 00:02:44.180
This is the Ground Self-Defense Force.

00:02:40.990 --> 00:02:42.560
Dear, you do the kitchen.

00:02:43.300 --> 00:02:46.830
Do you really think packing tape will stop a virus?

00:02:46.830 --> 00:02:48.730
Well, it's better than doing nothing!

00:02:48.730 --> 00:02:50.670
Just do it.

00:02:50.670 --> 00:02:51.690
Jeez.

00:02:53.180 --> 00:02:55.690
What the hell is going on?

00:03:18.860 --> 00:03:21.200
Oh, Keiichi-kun!

00:03:21.200 --> 00:03:22.630
Hey, Rena.

00:03:22.630 --> 00:03:24.500
I'm glad to see that you're safe.

00:03:24.500 --> 00:03:25.250
Yup.

00:03:25.250 --> 00:03:27.090
What about Satoko and Rika-chan?

00:03:27.090 --> 00:03:30.240
Rika-chan and the others live in a different district,

00:03:30.240 --> 00:03:32.690
so they have a different assembly place, I think.

00:03:33.330 --> 00:03:36.980
But I can't contact them to find out because the phone lines are down.

00:03:37.300 --> 00:03:40.110
So the phones don't work where you are either?

00:03:40.110 --> 00:03:43.120
I heard that an out-of-control car hit one of the telephone poles

00:03:43.120 --> 00:03:46.370
and brought down the lines.

00:03:46.370 --> 00:03:48.030
Seriously?

00:03:48.030 --> 00:03:49.620
Kei-chan!

00:03:51.560 --> 00:03:54.630
I'm so glad to see you two are all right!

00:03:54.630 --> 00:03:57.490
I'm just so happy!

00:03:57.490 --> 00:03:58.710
Hey!

00:03:58.710 --> 00:04:00.630
That hurts, Mi-chan.

00:04:01.020 --> 00:04:06.740
So has this virus really infected everyone in town?

00:04:06.740 --> 00:04:09.890
That scenario seems quite unlikely.

00:04:09.890 --> 00:04:12.890
The first victim was apparently from Takatsudo.

00:04:12.890 --> 00:04:15.750
But since the virus there was contained pretty quickly,

00:04:15.750 --> 00:04:18.970
they said it's not likely that the infection has reached our area.

00:04:18.970 --> 00:04:20.050
Then...

00:04:20.050 --> 00:04:24.350
Yeah. If we could ascertain that no one in Hinamizawa is infected,

00:04:24.350 --> 00:04:29.000
there's some optimism that they
could gradually lift the quarantine.

00:04:29.000 --> 00:04:30.540
I hope so.

00:04:31.190 --> 00:04:34.170
But I don't think I can be so optimistic.

00:04:36.170 --> 00:04:39.390
See, Uncle Mion here knows how to work a radio.

00:04:39.390 --> 00:04:43.890
I modified one to make it possible to listen to the police and Ground Forces channels.

00:04:43.890 --> 00:04:45.790
Isn't that illegal?

00:04:45.790 --> 00:04:47.680
Desperate times, desperate measures.

00:04:47.680 --> 00:04:50.500
From what I've intercepted so far,

00:04:50.500 --> 00:04:54.010
it seems this person has no history of traveling overseas,

00:04:54.010 --> 00:04:57.730
so they suspect there was a different original carrier.

00:04:57.730 --> 00:04:59.320
They're looking into that now.

00:04:59.320 --> 00:05:05.630
So basically, someone <i>else</i> caught it overseas and then brought it back to Hinamizawa.

00:05:05.630 --> 00:05:06.860
Or...

00:05:06.860 --> 00:05:10.980
it's possible that someone made contact with a carrier in another town and brought it back.

00:05:10.980 --> 00:05:12.980
From what I can discern,

00:05:12.980 --> 00:05:17.790
the quarantined area's too big for just
Hinamizawa. It must cover the entire region.

00:05:18.710 --> 00:05:19.790
Also...

00:05:20.480 --> 00:05:22.590
Keep what I'm about to say a secret.

00:05:25.460 --> 00:05:29.300
From what I've intercepted on the radio, in all this fuss about a virus

00:05:29.300 --> 00:05:33.100
it seems like they've turned to suspecting it could be a local disease from Hinamizawa.

00:05:33.100 --> 00:05:39.180
A local disease? You're saying <i>this</i> killer virus is different than the African virus?

00:05:39.180 --> 00:05:40.860
Could it be...

00:05:41.420 --> 00:05:44.490
Yes. Oyashiro-sama's curse.

00:05:44.490 --> 00:05:46.490
What, <i>that</i>?

00:05:47.670 --> 00:05:48.650
Yes.

00:05:48.650 --> 00:05:50.700
It's an old Hinamizawa legend:

00:05:50.700 --> 00:05:54.540
an impure <i>something</i> arose from the
Onigafuchi Swamp and attacked the village.

00:05:54.540 --> 00:05:55.750
You know the story.

00:05:55.750 --> 00:05:57.450
But Mi-chan.

00:05:57.450 --> 00:06:01.220
Back then, the village wasn't destroyed, right?

00:06:01.220 --> 00:06:05.760
Which means, it's not as deadly as the one they're talking about on TV,

00:06:05.760 --> 00:06:08.880
which could wipe out Hinamizawa.

00:06:08.880 --> 00:06:10.010
Is that true?

00:06:11.270 --> 00:06:12.510
According to the legend,

00:06:12.950 --> 00:06:16.220
if you got caught up in the impure substance from the swamp,

00:06:16.220 --> 00:06:20.090
you would transform into a demon, beyond the help of any person,

00:06:20.090 --> 00:06:23.100
and there would be no possible way to cure you until Oyashiro-sama himself descended.

00:06:27.060 --> 00:06:30.990
Which means if a miracle occurred like the one described in the legend,

00:06:30.990 --> 00:06:34.560
Hinamizawa could escape this disaster!

00:06:34.560 --> 00:06:35.370
In other words...

00:06:35.760 --> 00:06:39.770
...if Rika-chan, the reincarnation of Oyashiro-sama, showed herself,

00:06:39.770 --> 00:06:42.540
and publicly denied the prospect of Hinamizawa being destroyed,

00:06:42.540 --> 00:06:44.550
maybe everyone would calm down.

00:06:44.550 --> 00:06:46.670
Then let's hurry and get her!

00:06:46.990 --> 00:06:52.210
My grandma is trying to explain
that to the Ground Forces right now.

00:06:52.210 --> 00:06:57.890
But it looks like outsiders can't understand just how important Rika-chan is to Hinamizawa.

00:06:59.380 --> 00:07:02.430
Well, even putting aside talk about Oyashiro-sama,

00:07:02.430 --> 00:07:06.730
I want to see for myself that
Rika-chan and Satoko are all right.

00:07:06.730 --> 00:07:07.820
Me too.

00:07:07.820 --> 00:07:09.060
Yeah.

00:07:11.320 --> 00:07:12.700
Cabinet Minister Matsuda

00:07:12.700 --> 00:07:16.830
has just recently been embroiled in a
scandal over his secretary's wages, but now—

00:07:17.330 --> 00:07:20.080
"But wait," you ask, "what's so great about this vacuum cleaner?"

00:07:20.580 --> 00:07:23.080
Here is this week's forecast.

00:07:23.630 --> 00:07:26.590
There's not much news about Hinamizawa.

00:07:26.590 --> 00:07:32.710
Something like a virus in the boondocks
won't stay in the headlines for very long.

00:07:32.710 --> 00:07:34.600
What's this country coming to?

00:07:41.850 --> 00:07:43.180
Keiichi-kun!

00:07:43.180 --> 00:07:45.520
Kei-chan, looks like you're all right.

00:07:45.520 --> 00:07:48.750
Glad to see you are as well.

00:07:48.750 --> 00:07:53.500
So, how did it go? Were you able to check on Rika-chan and Satoko?

00:07:53.500 --> 00:07:54.370
Yeah.

00:07:54.370 --> 00:07:56.620
I heard this on the radio, but...

00:07:56.620 --> 00:08:00.300
Truth is, they've labeled Rika as "condition unknown" and apparently brought her in for examination.

00:08:00.300 --> 00:08:01.410
No way!

00:08:01.410 --> 00:08:05.350
Does that mean Rika-chan's got the virus?

00:08:05.350 --> 00:08:07.370
Shh, you're being too loud.

00:08:09.100 --> 00:08:10.620
S-Sorry.

00:08:11.880 --> 00:08:14.260
I don't know if it's the virus or not.

00:08:14.260 --> 00:08:18.430
In any case, she's been taken by the
quarantine corps and hasn't returned.

00:08:18.430 --> 00:08:21.100
How long has it been since she was taken?

00:08:21.100 --> 00:08:23.090
Since the day the quarantine began.

00:08:23.090 --> 00:08:24.960
Is Satoko-chan with her?

00:08:24.960 --> 00:08:26.890
I couldn't find that out.

00:08:26.890 --> 00:08:32.070
'Course not. Everyone in Hinamizawa completely ignores Satoko, after all.

00:08:35.110 --> 00:08:36.800
If someone comes down with the disease,

00:08:36.800 --> 00:08:40.830
normally the next step in a quarantine would be to confine their housemates.

00:08:40.830 --> 00:08:42.620
From what I hear on the radio,

00:08:42.620 --> 00:08:44.980
the only person who's being held is Rika-chan.

00:08:44.980 --> 00:08:48.150
So... this is getting pretty strange.

00:08:48.150 --> 00:08:49.540
In what way?

00:08:50.310 --> 00:08:54.460
Well, you know that Satoko's parents advocated for the dam, right?

00:08:54.460 --> 00:08:58.100
And so, they received divine punishment
from Oyashiro-sama and died in an accident.

00:08:58.100 --> 00:08:58.900
Yeah.

00:08:58.900 --> 00:09:03.400
So, the radicals are saying that
this time, Oyashiro-sama's curse

00:09:03.400 --> 00:09:05.810
has been brought on by Satoko.

00:09:05.810 --> 00:09:07.500
That's goddamn ridiculous.

00:09:07.500 --> 00:09:10.190
They blame <i>everything</i> on Satoko.

00:09:10.670 --> 00:09:19.200
TL Note: Wrapping someone in a bamboo mat and throwing them in a river
to drown was an established method of execution used in the Edo period.

00:09:10.670 --> 00:09:14.060
Some people are actually buying into the rumor that by wrapping Satoko in a mat

00:09:14.060 --> 00:09:19.200
and throwing her into the Onigafuchi Swamp, it would quell Oyashiro-sama's anger.

00:09:19.200 --> 00:09:20.990
That can't be!

00:09:21.540 --> 00:09:23.010
Damn.

00:09:23.010 --> 00:09:27.100
So Satoko is all alone, living in that storage house right now?

00:09:27.100 --> 00:09:28.380
That's dangerous!

00:09:28.380 --> 00:09:32.970
Right. There's a limit to what
Satoko-chan can do by herself.

00:09:32.970 --> 00:09:36.630
Shouldn't we hide her with us? Shouldn't we?

00:09:36.630 --> 00:09:39.080
But whose house should she stay at?

00:09:39.080 --> 00:09:42.620
I think my house would be even more dangerous for her.

00:09:42.620 --> 00:09:44.520
I'll hide her at my house.

00:09:45.960 --> 00:09:49.270
It'll be okay. I'll convince my dad.

00:09:49.520 --> 00:09:54.560
Okay. If we can contact Satoko,
we'll tell her to come to your house.

00:09:54.560 --> 00:09:56.240
Hold on a second.

00:09:56.730 --> 00:09:59.820
This doesn't just affect Satoko.

00:09:59.820 --> 00:10:03.290
Depending on the situation,
you two might be in danger too.

00:10:04.290 --> 00:10:05.660
What do you mean?

00:10:05.660 --> 00:10:08.040
I told you this before.

00:10:08.040 --> 00:10:12.580
About the rumor that this virus is
actually an old one from this village.

00:10:12.580 --> 00:10:15.150
That it gushed from the swamp, right?

00:10:15.150 --> 00:10:16.550
Yeah.

00:10:16.550 --> 00:10:20.930
And that everyone here has already been infected with it since ancient times.

00:10:20.930 --> 00:10:24.930
If that's true, then why haven't
people been dying from it all this time?

00:10:25.820 --> 00:10:34.940
The people who believe this rumor say that as long as the virus remains in Hinamizawa, it's stable. Harmless.

00:10:34.940 --> 00:10:38.000
The families that have been here for a while

00:10:38.000 --> 00:10:41.200
must have built up a generational immunity to it or something.

00:10:41.200 --> 00:10:45.160
Are they saying this is all because people who moved here from the outside,

00:10:45.160 --> 00:10:47.700
like Rena and I, don't have this immunity?

00:10:47.700 --> 00:10:49.900
That's exactly it!

00:10:49.900 --> 00:10:52.800
It's the fault of the outsiders who moved in here.

00:10:52.800 --> 00:10:58.630
They broke the fragile balance here, and caused the dormant virus in the villagers to act up!

00:10:58.630 --> 00:10:59.220
Um...

00:10:59.220 --> 00:11:03.600
You don't believe that ridiculous story, do you, Mi-chan?

00:11:03.600 --> 00:11:05.230
Of course I don't!

00:11:05.230 --> 00:11:09.100
There's no way that kind of nonsense holds any water!

00:11:09.100 --> 00:11:13.110
Normally, no one would believe such a stupid story.

00:11:14.340 --> 00:11:17.320
But lately everyone's gone crazy.

00:11:17.320 --> 00:11:20.240
False rumors like that are readily being swallowed,

00:11:20.240 --> 00:11:24.400
and if you attempt to refute them,
you're treated like an infected person.

00:11:24.400 --> 00:11:27.380
It's gotten really bad.

00:11:27.380 --> 00:11:32.950
So, Kei-chan, Rena, be careful.

00:11:36.330 --> 00:11:39.690
Don't let down your guard no matter what.

00:11:39.690 --> 00:11:40.380
Okay?

00:11:40.380 --> 00:11:41.940
Y-Yeah.

00:11:41.940 --> 00:11:43.390
Got it.

00:11:49.890 --> 00:11:52.690
I hope I'll be first in line today too.

00:11:58.330 --> 00:11:59.720
Huh?

00:11:59.720 --> 00:12:02.400
Where did everyone go?

00:12:09.560 --> 00:12:12.410
That's weird. I'm not picking up anything.

00:12:13.090 --> 00:12:14.920
What's going on?

00:12:29.530 --> 00:12:30.870
The hell's going on?!

00:12:30.870 --> 00:12:32.330
What's the meaning of this?

00:12:32.330 --> 00:12:33.460
Where's the water truck?

00:12:33.460 --> 00:12:35.190
What about doctors and supplies?

00:12:37.220 --> 00:12:39.440
We are the Ground Self-Defense Force.

00:12:39.960 --> 00:12:43.570
We will not allow you to leave the quarantined area.

00:12:43.570 --> 00:12:46.450
Turn around and return to your homes.

00:12:46.450 --> 00:12:47.950
Don't give me that!

00:12:47.950 --> 00:12:49.700
Are you abandoning us?!

00:12:49.700 --> 00:12:53.020
How are we supposed to survive without food and water?

00:12:53.020 --> 00:12:55.080
Hey, answer us!

00:12:57.730 --> 00:13:01.840
If you do not depart immediately, we shall shoot without hesitation.

00:13:19.360 --> 00:13:21.300
That's strange.

00:13:21.300 --> 00:13:23.600
Why isn't the TV working?

00:13:24.710 --> 00:13:26.110
What's going on?

00:13:28.620 --> 00:13:32.510
Nothing's coming in on this radio.

00:13:32.510 --> 00:13:33.870
Keiichi?

00:13:33.870 --> 00:13:36.870
There's a letter for you here.

00:13:38.100 --> 00:13:39.550
A letter?

00:13:39.550 --> 00:13:41.130
For me?

00:13:42.560 --> 00:13:45.880
It was pushed into the crack of the door.

00:13:46.480 --> 00:13:47.560
Thanks.

00:13:47.560 --> 00:13:48.500
Uh huh.

00:13:49.020 --> 00:13:51.090
What was Mion thinking?

00:13:52.020 --> 00:13:53.890
She should have just come by in person.

00:13:53.890 --> 00:13:55.300
Let's see...

00:13:55.300 --> 00:13:56.490
<i>To Kei-chan.</i>

00:13:56.490 --> 00:13:57.800
<i>Be careful!</i>

00:13:57.800 --> 00:14:00.860
<i>The Neighborhood Association is strongly considering</i>

00:14:00.860 --> 00:14:04.400
<i>making an example of the
Maebara and Ryuuguu families.</i>

00:14:04.400 --> 00:14:06.920
Wh-What does she mean by that?!

00:14:07.650 --> 00:14:09.960
<i>If anyone tries to stop them, they'll say it's because you're protecting them,</i>

00:14:09.960 --> 00:14:14.660
<i>because you too are an infected person, or so goes their twisted logic.</i>

00:14:14.660 --> 00:14:17.690
<i>Talk of lynching your families has gotten out of hand.</i>

00:14:17.690 --> 00:14:21.650
<i>If my grandma were healthy,
she'd put a stop to this madness.</i>

00:14:21.650 --> 00:14:24.300
<i>But a few days ago, she came down with a high fever</i>

00:14:24.300 --> 00:14:26.720
<i>and is now unable to even sit up. </i>

00:14:26.720 --> 00:14:29.990
<i>A few of my relatives are even saying that she's become infected herself,</i>

00:14:29.990 --> 00:14:32.830
<i>which puts me in an uncertain position when I speak for the household...</i>

00:14:32.830 --> 00:14:38.250
<i>Rather, if I mess up in any way,
I'll certainly pay for it with my life.</i>

00:14:38.250 --> 00:14:43.440
<i>Under these circumstances, I can no
longer protect your family or Rena's.</i>

00:14:44.300 --> 00:14:47.940
<i>Grandma says that this situation is
almost a play-by-play reenactment</i>

00:14:47.940 --> 00:14:52.520
<i>of the old legend where the demons came out of Onigafuchi Swamp.</i>

00:14:52.520 --> 00:14:57.910
<i>She says that it's turning into a hell where everyone wants to kill everyone else.</i>

00:14:58.000 --> 00:15:02.320
<i>I think it's too dangerous for you to stay in Hinamizawa any longer.</i>

00:15:02.320 --> 00:15:08.470
<i>At the very least, if we continue to stay shut up in our houses, we'll eventually wind up dead!</i>

00:15:08.840 --> 00:15:13.920
<i>That's why I'm planning to escape from here tomorrow night.</i>

00:15:13.920 --> 00:15:17.180
<i>The Sonozaki family owns a few secret tunnels. </i>

00:15:17.180 --> 00:15:21.120
<i>One of them leads out beyond the blockade lines.</i>

00:15:21.120 --> 00:15:24.810
<i>Tonight, talk to your family and have them prepare to leave.</i>

00:15:24.810 --> 00:15:27.730
<i>Come and meet me tomorrow night, and we'll all get out of here!</i>

00:15:28.300 --> 00:15:31.200
<i>I've sent the same letter to Rena.</i>

00:15:31.200 --> 00:15:35.930
<i>I know this all sounds pretty crazy, but please believe me!</i>

00:15:35.930 --> 00:15:39.000
<i>Though, even if you believe me and we act on this plan,</i>

00:15:39.580 --> 00:15:45.220
<i>I estimate our chances of escaping
Hinamizawa to be around only 10% at best.</i>

00:15:46.250 --> 00:15:48.000
I-Is that all there is?

00:15:48.570 --> 00:15:51.010
Is this for real?

00:15:55.310 --> 00:15:57.140
What about Satoko?

00:15:57.140 --> 00:15:59.950
Rika-chan is one thing, but Satoko...

00:16:01.140 --> 00:16:02.190
What was that?

00:16:07.690 --> 00:16:09.530
Wh-What?!

00:16:19.120 --> 00:16:20.700
Wh-Who is it?

00:16:20.700 --> 00:16:22.750
It's Ryuuguu. Please open the door!

00:16:22.750 --> 00:16:23.710
Hurry!

00:16:23.710 --> 00:16:25.090
It's Rena!

00:16:25.090 --> 00:16:25.580
Hey!

00:16:27.630 --> 00:16:28.560
Huh?!

00:16:30.020 --> 00:16:31.650
Wh-What?!

00:16:30.600 --> 00:16:31.650
M-Mion!

00:16:31.650 --> 00:16:32.500
Are you okay?

00:16:32.500 --> 00:16:34.090
Of course she isn't!

00:16:34.090 --> 00:16:35.270
We need to stop the bleeding!

00:16:35.270 --> 00:16:36.950
D-Dear! We need to treat her!

00:16:37.780 --> 00:16:39.390
Rena, what happe—

00:16:41.850 --> 00:16:43.890
What the hell happened?!

00:16:47.640 --> 00:16:48.400
R-Rena!

00:16:58.990 --> 00:17:00.260
It hurts!

00:17:05.370 --> 00:17:06.850
Stop!

00:17:06.850 --> 00:17:07.980
Please stop!

00:17:07.980 --> 00:17:12.850
If you want to kill someone, you
should be prepared to die yourself!

00:17:12.850 --> 00:17:14.840
Don't take that responsibility lightly!

00:17:19.890 --> 00:17:21.060
R-Rena...

00:17:21.060 --> 00:17:23.020
That one's still alive!

00:17:32.520 --> 00:17:34.240
S-Sorry.

00:17:34.240 --> 00:17:35.110
It's okay.

00:17:35.110 --> 00:17:37.530
More importantly, we have to get ready to escape.

00:17:37.530 --> 00:17:38.280
R-Right.

00:17:38.280 --> 00:17:39.990
But tell me something!

00:17:39.990 --> 00:17:41.540
What happened?!

00:17:42.820 --> 00:17:46.300
Mi-chan brought a letter to my house too.

00:17:46.300 --> 00:17:49.040
But she was found by the vigilantes and shot!

00:17:49.400 --> 00:17:53.220
She was shot only for having
brought a letter to my house.

00:17:53.990 --> 00:17:56.300
They decided that we Ryuuguus were infected

00:17:56.300 --> 00:18:01.030
and anyone who had contact with us was helping us out.

00:18:01.030 --> 00:18:03.560
So they shot her, just like that.

00:18:12.530 --> 00:18:14.880
Rena-chan, that gun...

00:18:14.880 --> 00:18:19.070
Even if you don't shoot a gun,
you can still intimidate people with it.

00:18:21.420 --> 00:18:25.020
Mr. Maebara, if we don't escape from here right now, we'll die.

00:18:25.020 --> 00:18:28.230
My father has already been killed.

00:18:28.230 --> 00:18:31.780
When he tried to help Mi-chan...

00:18:31.780 --> 00:18:33.950
They didn't hesitate.

00:18:33.950 --> 00:18:38.390
They shot people as easily as
shooting at birds to drive them away.

00:18:38.390 --> 00:18:40.270
S-Sorry, Rena.

00:18:40.270 --> 00:18:42.450
If only I hadn't messed up...

00:18:42.450 --> 00:18:43.220
Sorry!

00:18:43.740 --> 00:18:45.440
It's not your fault.

00:18:45.440 --> 00:18:48.850
And I don't hate anybody.

00:18:48.850 --> 00:18:53.360
I've already settled the score with the people who deserve my hatred.

00:18:54.240 --> 00:18:56.970
Anyway, let's get ready to go!

00:18:56.970 --> 00:18:58.740
More of them will be coming any minute now!

00:18:58.740 --> 00:19:01.740
O-Okay. Let's do that!

00:19:02.110 --> 00:19:06.120
I'll slow everyone down, so leave me here.

00:19:06.120 --> 00:19:10.590
We can't. Without you, we won't be able to find the secret tunnel.

00:19:10.590 --> 00:19:13.220
You can't just carelessly abandon your responsibilities.

00:19:13.220 --> 00:19:14.630
Lead us there!

00:19:16.610 --> 00:19:18.710
You got me.

00:19:18.710 --> 00:19:22.170
You won't let me die in peace, will you?

00:19:22.170 --> 00:19:27.330
Hey, Mi-chan. We don't have time for
chit-chat right now, so be straight with me.

00:19:28.380 --> 00:19:32.400
Why are you asking us to leave Satoko-chan behind and escape by ourselves?

00:19:32.400 --> 00:19:35.640
That's right! I was wondering that too.

00:19:35.640 --> 00:19:37.280
What's going to happen to Satoko?

00:19:37.760 --> 00:19:43.120
Apparently, a little while ago
Satoko was taken away on a boat.

00:19:43.120 --> 00:19:47.840
She's to be the sacrifice for the
ceremony from the legend of Onigafuchi.

00:19:47.840 --> 00:19:51.040
They intend to drown her at the end of a three-day ritual.

00:19:51.040 --> 00:19:52.530
But she's still alive, right?

00:19:52.530 --> 00:19:53.500
She <i>is</i>, right?

00:19:54.790 --> 00:19:57.100
There's nothing we can do.

00:19:57.100 --> 00:19:59.050
We can't do anything!

00:20:01.560 --> 00:20:05.820
With the Shrine Association and the
Young Men's Association on their side,

00:20:05.820 --> 00:20:08.200
we're up against over a hundred people.

00:20:08.200 --> 00:20:11.060
They even roped in the Hunters Association.

00:20:11.060 --> 00:20:14.570
And they're armed with more than 20 hunting guns.

00:20:14.570 --> 00:20:20.470
While chanting Oyashiro-sama's name,
they've all been taken by a fog of madness.

00:20:20.470 --> 00:20:22.240
They're merciless.

00:20:22.240 --> 00:20:25.820
Anybody who tries to stop them is murdered in cold blood.

00:20:28.490 --> 00:20:31.410
They were completely normal just a while ago.

00:20:32.260 --> 00:20:34.210
Then, all of a sudden, they went crazy.

00:20:34.970 --> 00:20:38.590
This virus drives people insane!

00:20:38.590 --> 00:20:43.360
And the legend of Oyashiro-sama is about to be reenacted!

00:20:43.360 --> 00:20:46.840
The only one who can do anything about this is Oyashiro-sama!

00:20:46.840 --> 00:20:50.410
Not Rika-chan, his reincarnation! And not us!

00:20:50.410 --> 00:20:54.640
Humans... Humans can't do anything!

00:20:54.640 --> 00:20:56.330
Nothing...

00:21:03.150 --> 00:21:05.200
Calm down, Mion.

00:21:07.450 --> 00:21:09.750
Thanks, Mion.

00:21:09.750 --> 00:21:14.240
While Rena and I didn't know
anything and were taking it easy,

00:21:14.240 --> 00:21:20.120
you put yourself through a lot of
trouble to lay those rumors to rest.

00:21:20.120 --> 00:21:26.890
If not for your efforts, we'd probably have long since been swallowed up by this insanity.

00:21:26.890 --> 00:21:29.240
So, thank you, Mion.

00:21:31.270 --> 00:21:34.520
Rena, you probably want to blame Mion for this, but...

00:21:34.950 --> 00:21:37.050
Not at all.

00:21:37.050 --> 00:21:39.110
Actually, I think this is good news.

00:21:39.110 --> 00:21:42.400
Yeah, without a doubt this is good news.

00:21:42.400 --> 00:21:45.400
Yup. Because Satoko-chan is alive!

00:21:45.400 --> 00:21:49.040
And on top of that, by waiting three days to drown her,

00:21:49.040 --> 00:21:53.070
that means that they'll make sure to keep her alive for the next 72 hours!

00:21:55.190 --> 00:21:58.330
Yeah, I get it, Satoshi.

00:21:58.330 --> 00:22:01.420
When even <i>you</i> get serious,
there's nothing to be afraid of.

00:22:01.970 --> 00:22:06.450
With a few whacks, this little guy can
give their faces one hell of a makeover!

00:22:06.450 --> 00:22:11.200
K-Keiichi! You aren't actually thinking of going to rescue Satoko-chan, are you?

00:22:11.200 --> 00:22:15.680
Dad, you take Mom and Mion
and escape out the back door.

00:22:15.680 --> 00:22:17.440
Rena and I will handle the rest.

00:22:17.810 --> 00:22:20.040
I apologize for the trouble.

00:22:20.040 --> 00:22:22.800
Please take good care of Mi-chan.

00:22:22.800 --> 00:22:31.070
Mi-chan likes to hog all the glory for herself, so she may try to tag along after us.

00:22:31.600 --> 00:22:34.200
Even though she's badly injured and it would be painful for her...

00:22:34.200 --> 00:22:35.840
Heh.

00:22:35.840 --> 00:22:39.190
Don't treat me like I'm a burden.

00:22:39.190 --> 00:22:42.710
Then let's meet at the Sonozaki house.

00:22:43.450 --> 00:22:45.840
You two should come escape with us!

00:22:45.840 --> 00:22:48.140
What can the two of you{ do against <i>them</i>?

00:22:48.140 --> 00:22:53.220
Thanks for your concern, but it's too late for that.

00:22:56.710 --> 00:22:58.800
Let's go, Keiichi-kun.

00:22:58.800 --> 00:22:59.830
Yeah.

00:23:00.210 --> 00:23:01.980
Well then, see ya in a few.

00:23:03.730 --> 00:23:05.740
I'm counting on you, Dad.

00:23:05.740 --> 00:23:07.400
You better come back.

00:23:07.400 --> 00:23:08.450
We will.

00:23:11.610 --> 00:23:14.670
So there's about 20 of them.

00:23:14.670 --> 00:23:17.770
Do they really think they can win?

00:23:17.770 --> 00:23:20.070
I'm sure they do.

00:23:20.070 --> 00:23:24.880
Like most amateurs, they probably think there's safety in numbers.

00:23:24.880 --> 00:23:27.100
What a bunch of idiots.

00:23:27.100 --> 00:23:31.270
If they had just stayed quietly at home, they could have lived longer lives.

00:23:31.270 --> 00:23:34.140
But they committed several grave errors.

00:23:34.140 --> 00:23:38.820
Yeah. They shot Mion. And kidnapped Satoko.

00:23:38.820 --> 00:23:44.530
It's a hell of a mistake to mess with our club.

00:23:46.150 --> 00:23:48.270
Hey, Keiichi-kun.

00:23:48.270 --> 00:23:53.590
When we were listening to Mi-chan's story, you said it was "good news".

00:23:53.590 --> 00:23:56.760
But I meant "good news" in a different way.

00:23:56.760 --> 00:23:58.790
In what way?

00:23:59.870 --> 00:24:03.140
We're up against the Shrine Association and the Young Men's Association.

00:24:03.140 --> 00:24:04.920
About 100 people, right?

00:24:04.920 --> 00:24:08.490
Well, well. Ain't that a lucky break for us?

00:24:08.490 --> 00:24:11.050
There's only 100 of them.

00:24:11.050 --> 00:24:13.050
On second thought, that's not enough at all.

00:24:13.050 --> 00:24:18.310
You said it. I wanna take out the whole of Hinamizawa right now.

00:24:18.310 --> 00:24:21.430
And there's about 20 of them right here.

00:24:21.430 --> 00:24:24.440
They really <i>are</i> underestimating us.

00:24:25.060 --> 00:24:27.410
Will we even be able to work up a sweat?

00:24:28.440 --> 00:24:31.950
Well, how about we just let loose and enjoy ourselves?

00:24:33.030 --> 00:24:35.200
Satoko-chan, wait for us!

00:24:57.740 --> 00:25:02.980
Before we discuss the η-173 virus, 

00:25:03.430 --> 00:25:07.650
we will explain the Class-C brain virus.

00:25:07.650 --> 00:25:08.950
Iwashi.

00:25:14.700 --> 00:25:18.860
The existence of parasitic Class-C
brain viruses, or simply "Class-Cs",

00:25:18.860 --> 00:25:22.810
has not been officially confirmed even into the present day.

00:25:22.810 --> 00:25:25.260
But according to an informal study by the UN,

00:25:25.260 --> 00:25:31.000
over 99% of humans are infected with a Class-C brain parasite.

00:25:31.440 --> 00:25:32.760
Hold it right there.

00:25:33.890 --> 00:25:34.510
Yes?

00:25:34.510 --> 00:25:41.260
99%, meaning... both you and I are infected with this virus?

00:25:41.260 --> 00:25:44.730
You may think of it that way.

00:25:44.730 --> 00:25:47.120
However, instead of calling it a virus,

00:25:47.120 --> 00:25:50.270
it's more accurate to think of it as a parasite.

00:25:50.270 --> 00:25:51.520
A parasite?

00:25:51.520 --> 00:25:55.080
As even the average person knows these days,

00:25:55.080 --> 00:25:57.840
we share a symbiotic relationship
with E. coli and other microorganisms.

00:25:57.840 --> 00:26:00.910
You may think of it as a similar sort of arrangement.

00:26:00.910 --> 00:26:03.660
Then there shouldn't be any problem.

00:26:04.250 --> 00:26:07.760
The problem lies in the suggested possibility

00:26:07.760 --> 00:26:11.670
of the virus altering the brain functions of the host.

00:26:12.920 --> 00:26:18.130
Class-C parasitic viruses are said to induce
amicable behavior toward hosts of the same virus

00:26:18.130 --> 00:26:24.930
and hostile behavior toward hosts of different Class-C parasitic viruses.

00:26:24.930 --> 00:26:26.720
What do you mean by that?

00:26:26.720 --> 00:26:30.680
Are you saying there are multiple variants of this virus?

00:26:31.200 --> 00:26:33.690
Several hundred strains are known to exist.

00:26:34.280 --> 00:26:35.520
Oddly enough,

00:26:35.520 --> 00:26:39.700
their distribution coincides with that of
national boundaries and religious groups.

00:26:41.200 --> 00:26:45.580
In other words, the differences between each country's culture and disposition

00:26:45.580 --> 00:26:49.710
are all derived from the hidden guidance of these viruses.

00:26:49.710 --> 00:26:54.500
Then are you saying that humanity has been guided by these viruses since ancient times?

00:26:55.490 --> 00:26:55.960
Yes.

00:26:55.960 --> 00:26:58.970
I-I can't believe what I'm hearing.

00:27:03.540 --> 00:27:07.060
The UN pushed for the eradication of the virus, but...

00:27:07.540 --> 00:27:10.000
some raised concerns that such efforts

00:27:10.000 --> 00:27:13.730
would spark ethnic cleansing programs like the one the Nazis carried out.

00:27:13.730 --> 00:27:20.990
As a result, research on the virus was forever forbidden, and the records were destroyed.

00:27:21.590 --> 00:27:25.490
The UN brushed aside the existence of the virus?

00:27:26.140 --> 00:27:31.680
But apparently, each country continued its own research into the virus.

00:27:31.680 --> 00:27:36.910
In our own country, a group of medical
institutions has been continuing secret research

00:27:36.910 --> 00:27:42.760
and is the organization behind the η-173 virus, which is our current problem. 

00:27:43.460 --> 00:27:46.580
In other words, the η-173 virus...

00:27:46.580 --> 00:27:54.360
...is a Class-C parasitic brain virus researched and developed by our own country.

00:27:55.760 --> 00:28:00.880
Even among Class-C viruses, this η-173
can produce drastic personality changes

00:28:00.880 --> 00:28:04.030
in an extremely short time.

00:28:04.630 --> 00:28:07.030
Drastic personality changes?

00:28:07.030 --> 00:28:10.290
It promotes aggression and paranoia.

00:28:10.290 --> 00:28:15.290
These tendencies are already becoming pronounced in the infected residents of the Hinamizawa area,

00:28:15.290 --> 00:28:21.300
and in a short time, mob violence and mass killings will manifest.

00:28:22.080 --> 00:28:27.180
A-And you're saying that <i>your </i>people
developed such a dreadful virus?

00:28:27.960 --> 00:28:30.680
I will explain the rest.

00:28:32.560 --> 00:28:36.660
Up till today, the research on the η-173
virus was conducted behind closed doors

00:28:36.660 --> 00:28:42.700
by the Alphabet Council, which has authority beyond the law.

00:28:43.270 --> 00:28:46.060
The next step was the challenge of mass manufacturing it cheaply

00:28:46.060 --> 00:28:49.700
and also stabilizing it enough to function as a biological weapon.

00:28:50.490 --> 00:28:51.940
A biological weapon?!

00:28:51.940 --> 00:28:53.090
You can't be serious!

00:28:53.090 --> 00:28:57.710
Are you saying that this country was developing a biological weapon?!

00:29:02.960 --> 00:29:05.980
Since this breach was caused by an unfortunate accident,

00:29:05.980 --> 00:29:09.940
at the same time as we give treatment to the citizens,

00:29:09.940 --> 00:29:12.980
we are planning to collect valuable data on how it affects humans.

00:29:13.610 --> 00:29:16.240
You're even going that far?!

00:29:16.240 --> 00:29:18.610
Who <i>are</i> you people?

00:29:18.610 --> 00:29:22.200
Our research on this matter will surely become valuable to this country,

00:29:22.200 --> 00:29:24.860
and I'm confident that it is in the national interest.

00:29:25.660 --> 00:29:29.620
You must give full authority over this matter to the Alphabet Project.

00:29:30.160 --> 00:29:33.500
Y-You are... the Alphabet Council's...

00:29:33.500 --> 00:29:34.600
Prime Minister.

00:29:34.600 --> 00:29:37.500
Order the Ground Forces to begin the quarantine.

00:29:47.620 --> 00:29:50.580
This is the Ground Self-Defense Force.

00:29:50.580 --> 00:29:53.170
As of 4 AM this morning,

00:29:53.170 --> 00:29:56.920
Hinamizawa and other areas
specified by the prefectural governor

00:29:56.920 --> 00:29:59.200
have been placed under quarantine.

00:29:59.200 --> 00:30:05.720
Until the safety of the quarantined area can be determined, you may not leave this district.

00:30:05.720 --> 00:30:11.150
Those who do not abide by this decree will be punished in accordance with national law.

00:30:11.150 --> 00:30:15.540
Please return to your homes and remain calm.

00:30:16.060 --> 00:30:19.380
This is the Emergency Response Headquarters.

00:30:19.380 --> 00:30:25.660
Beginning at noon today, there will be a mass
medical examination at the designated locations.

00:30:22.170 --> 00:30:25.670
Why's it so loud this early?

00:30:25.660 --> 00:30:30.660
Please follow the instructions of your
local representatives and gather there.

00:30:26.390 --> 00:30:29.050
Rika, what's going on?

00:30:29.510 --> 00:30:31.100
All this noise...

00:30:35.220 --> 00:30:36.930
Rika?

00:30:53.710 --> 00:30:55.610
We'll start with an examination of the subject's blood.

00:30:55.610 --> 00:30:57.720
Then we'll perform bone marrow aspiration.

00:30:57.720 --> 00:30:58.580
We're all set up.

00:31:05.290 --> 00:31:06.800
What's going on?

00:31:06.800 --> 00:31:11.280
Why isn't the preventative medicine against η- 173 showing any effect?

00:31:11.280 --> 00:31:15.280
At this rate, there will be a rapid increase in the number of stage L5 patients.

00:31:15.280 --> 00:31:20.730
There are reports that even some among the
Ground Forces are exhibiting symptoms of infection.

00:31:21.260 --> 00:31:23.620
This is moving way too fast.

00:31:23.620 --> 00:31:27.280
It shouldn't be possible for the
infection to spread this quickly!

00:31:31.690 --> 00:31:37.650
Four of the unit members tested positive for η-173 in the latest regular blood test.

00:31:37.650 --> 00:31:43.670
From this, it is clear that the protective equipment we currently use is ineffective against this virus.

00:31:43.670 --> 00:31:46.080
Therefore, the disaster relief unit

00:31:46.080 --> 00:31:50.300
will withdraw from the quarantined area effective immediately.

00:31:53.640 --> 00:31:56.440
Experimental Equipment Company 738

00:31:56.440 --> 00:32:01.190
will hereby be placed under the authority of the Hinamizawa disaster relief operation.

00:32:01.190 --> 00:32:06.360
Troops are to immediately dispatch and
maintain public order in the quarantined zone.

00:32:06.360 --> 00:32:09.900
As per regulations, you are authorized to use live ammunition during the operation.

00:32:39.100 --> 00:32:45.130
How? How did the virus evolve this quickly?

00:32:51.400 --> 00:32:54.380
There's nothing left to be done.

00:32:54.380 --> 00:32:56.070
Humans can't do anything...

00:32:57.450 --> 00:33:00.570
Humanity is already...

00:33:15.430 --> 00:33:18.300
Die!

00:33:22.140 --> 00:33:23.890
Ow!

00:33:33.150 --> 00:33:35.470
Are you okay, Rena?

00:33:35.990 --> 00:33:37.780
Thanks, Keiichi-kun.

00:33:44.790 --> 00:33:46.810
Mi-chan, wait for us.

00:33:46.810 --> 00:33:49.230
We'll definitely bring Satoko-chan back with us.

00:33:49.230 --> 00:33:50.670
Let's go, Rena.

00:34:08.320 --> 00:34:10.620
Dear, come on.

00:34:10.620 --> 00:34:13.730
Will those kids really come?

00:34:13.730 --> 00:34:17.820
How... How did it all end up like this?

00:34:17.820 --> 00:34:21.830
It's okay. You don't need to
worry about Kei-chan and Rena.

00:34:21.830 --> 00:34:27.330
They'll definitely rescue Satoko and meet up with us.

00:34:27.330 --> 00:34:30.120
How can you be so sure?

00:34:30.120 --> 00:34:35.050
Because they're the aces of my club.

00:34:35.050 --> 00:34:37.590
They'll definitely come back.

00:34:44.600 --> 00:34:48.300
Are they keeping Satoko in that cabin?

00:34:48.300 --> 00:34:52.240
Look. There are lights on the
path along Onigafuchi Swamp.

00:34:52.240 --> 00:34:52.860
Yeah.

00:34:53.240 --> 00:34:55.740
We <i>could</i> just burst in,

00:34:55.740 --> 00:34:59.440
but let's use the strategy that has the
best chance of safely rescuing Satoko.

00:34:59.440 --> 00:35:00.240
What do you propose?

00:35:00.240 --> 00:35:03.380
Although they seem to be getting along nicely,

00:35:03.380 --> 00:35:07.390
at this point they probably
don't trust each other anymore.

00:35:07.390 --> 00:35:08.640
We'll use that against them.

00:35:08.640 --> 00:35:09.910
I see.

00:35:09.910 --> 00:35:13.530
Keiichi-kun, you never fail to disappoint. So you're going to spread some rumors.

00:35:13.530 --> 00:35:15.870
Our club was the perfect training ground for it.

00:35:15.870 --> 00:35:17.760
This'll be a piece of cake!

00:35:23.180 --> 00:35:24.510
Bad news!

00:35:25.080 --> 00:35:29.910
The guys from the next district are
coming to capture the Houjou girl!

00:35:29.910 --> 00:35:31.200
What?

00:35:31.200 --> 00:35:32.520
What do you mean?!

00:35:32.960 --> 00:35:38.030
There's a rumor spreading that if you drink that girl's lifeblood, you'll be saved!

00:35:38.030 --> 00:35:41.600
Those idiots, believing a rumor like that!

00:35:41.600 --> 00:35:43.250
Wh-What should we do?

00:35:43.250 --> 00:35:47.740
We're about to start the sacrificial ceremony! We can't give her up!

00:35:47.740 --> 00:35:50.350
Like we care if they're from the next district over!

00:35:50.350 --> 00:35:51.930
They're just dirty rats!

00:35:54.540 --> 00:35:55.860
Let's get 'em!

00:35:57.160 --> 00:35:58.440
This is bad!

00:35:58.440 --> 00:36:02.800
The guys from the next district over are
heading to the cabin to take away Houjou!

00:36:02.800 --> 00:36:06.290
What? Shit, just where are they coming from?

00:36:06.290 --> 00:36:07.640
Who cares?

00:36:08.060 --> 00:36:09.760
In any case, we can't give her up!

00:36:09.760 --> 00:36:10.950
Let's go back to the cabin!

00:36:10.950 --> 00:36:12.320
Yeah!

00:36:19.740 --> 00:36:22.070
Wh-Who's there? Is someone there?

00:36:36.710 --> 00:36:38.050
They're coming!

00:36:38.050 --> 00:36:39.710
Not yet. Don't shoot yet!

00:36:41.720 --> 00:36:44.620
Hey! What do you want?

00:36:45.160 --> 00:36:47.850
We've come to protect the Houjou girl!

00:36:48.420 --> 00:36:49.850
What district are you from?

00:36:51.800 --> 00:36:53.900
Bastards, don't fuck with us!

00:36:53.900 --> 00:36:55.100
Shoot 'em dead!

00:36:58.650 --> 00:37:01.180
Dammit! Were we too late?

00:37:01.180 --> 00:37:04.490
Listen, we're gonna take back the girl!

00:37:07.870 --> 00:37:10.860
Good. Now the cabin will be poorly guarded.

00:37:10.860 --> 00:37:11.680
Let's go.

00:37:11.680 --> 00:37:12.120
Yeah.

00:37:17.540 --> 00:37:20.130
What is happening out there?

00:37:25.260 --> 00:37:26.650
Assholes!

00:37:26.650 --> 00:37:27.640
K-Kill them!

00:37:35.560 --> 00:37:36.940
You!

00:37:36.940 --> 00:37:38.060
You bastards!

00:37:51.690 --> 00:37:53.830
Satoko!

00:37:53.830 --> 00:37:54.900
Keiichi-san?

00:37:54.900 --> 00:37:57.040
Satoko-chan, wait for us!

00:37:57.040 --> 00:37:58.020
Rena-san too?

00:38:03.010 --> 00:38:07.760
Don't move! If you come any closer, I'll blow her head off!

00:38:07.760 --> 00:38:09.230
Satoko-chan!

00:38:09.230 --> 00:38:10.180
Satoko!

00:38:10.640 --> 00:38:12.260
Rena-san! Keiichi-san!

00:38:12.260 --> 00:38:16.890
Don't worry! We'll take these guys down and rescue you!

00:38:17.920 --> 00:38:20.400
You're the ones who are going down!

00:38:20.820 --> 00:38:24.900
You are fools for risking your lives just for me!

00:38:25.270 --> 00:38:26.890
Yeah, we are.

00:38:26.890 --> 00:38:30.250
Both Rena and I are huge idiots.

00:38:30.250 --> 00:38:35.040
But do you have a problem with that, Satoko?

00:38:36.890 --> 00:38:38.080
No, I don't.

00:38:38.080 --> 00:38:41.670
Stop talking and chew lead!

00:38:44.980 --> 00:38:46.300
You damned brat!

00:38:47.800 --> 00:38:48.820
Bitch!

00:38:53.150 --> 00:38:54.620
Dammit!

00:38:54.620 --> 00:38:55.480
Satoko-chan!

00:38:59.340 --> 00:39:00.300
Rena-san!

00:39:01.020 --> 00:39:03.550
Rena-san! Rena-san!

00:39:03.550 --> 00:39:04.830
Screw you!

00:39:04.830 --> 00:39:07.060
You can die too!

00:39:10.650 --> 00:39:11.740
Keiichi-san!

00:39:14.180 --> 00:39:15.120
Keiichi-kun!

00:39:16.510 --> 00:39:19.250
You can all die together!

00:39:22.720 --> 00:39:24.550
Don't even!

00:39:36.270 --> 00:39:37.350
Keiichi-kun!

00:39:37.350 --> 00:39:38.260
Keiichi-san!

00:39:38.880 --> 00:39:41.170
That was a shock.

00:39:41.170 --> 00:39:43.500
I thought I was dead for a moment there.

00:39:43.500 --> 00:39:45.690
You weren't shot?

00:39:45.690 --> 00:39:48.900
I <i>was</i> shot, but Satoshi saved me.

00:39:53.890 --> 00:39:55.530
Nii-nii did?

00:39:55.530 --> 00:39:56.310
Yeah.

00:39:56.310 --> 00:39:58.040
I owe you one, Satoshi.

00:39:58.960 --> 00:40:03.670
Why? Why did you risk your lives just for me?

00:40:04.300 --> 00:40:06.420
We made a promise to Mion.

00:40:06.420 --> 00:40:07.650
Yeah.

00:40:07.650 --> 00:40:09.920
We told her we'd definitely bring you back.

00:40:10.420 --> 00:40:12.480
Keiichi-san...

00:40:12.480 --> 00:40:13.820
Rena-san...

00:40:22.010 --> 00:40:25.550
Keiichi-san, what about Rika?

00:40:26.520 --> 00:40:31.450
Sorry. We have no idea where Rika-chan is.

00:40:31.450 --> 00:40:34.820
So we're just leaving her behind and escaping on our own?

00:40:34.820 --> 00:40:38.900
Listen, Satoko-chan. Rika-chan is different than the rest of us.

00:40:38.900 --> 00:40:45.030
Rika-chan is Oyashiro-sama's reincarnation. Even if she stays here, she won't be harmed.

00:40:45.030 --> 00:40:48.100
So for now, we'll escape without her.

00:40:48.100 --> 00:40:51.410
When things calm down, we'll definitely come back for her.

00:40:51.410 --> 00:40:52.840
That's...

00:40:52.840 --> 00:40:54.630
We don't have a choice.

00:40:54.630 --> 00:40:56.700
Mion was shot and is badly wounded.

00:40:56.700 --> 00:41:01.470
And our chances of getting killed keep going up the longer we stay here.

00:41:01.470 --> 00:41:03.850
So, so...

00:41:05.060 --> 00:41:06.960
I understand.

00:41:06.960 --> 00:41:08.550
Sorry.

00:41:08.550 --> 00:41:11.860
But can we stop by just one place first?

00:41:11.860 --> 00:41:13.370
Where?

00:41:13.370 --> 00:41:15.440
My house.

00:41:15.440 --> 00:41:19.490
Because I can't have you keep carrying me on your back.

00:41:19.920 --> 00:41:22.500
I'd like to go get my shoes.

00:41:23.290 --> 00:41:28.000
Plus, Rika may have come back...

00:41:28.000 --> 00:41:30.390
Okay. Let's get a move on.

00:41:30.390 --> 00:41:31.510
Yeah.

00:41:44.830 --> 00:41:48.690
Child of man, the time for our parting has come.

00:41:48.690 --> 00:41:50.250
It would seem so.

00:41:50.250 --> 00:41:53.280
But isn't it too early?

00:41:53.280 --> 00:41:56.950
Yes. <i>We're</i> still too young.

00:41:58.090 --> 00:42:04.280
It would have taken more than a
thousand years for <i>us</i> to accept this planet.

00:42:04.280 --> 00:42:07.220
Hinamizawa was supposed to be the shell of an egg

00:42:07.220 --> 00:42:10.290
that should have warmly protected us until that time.

00:42:11.040 --> 00:42:14.040
Humans were the ones who broke it.

00:42:14.040 --> 00:42:16.300
It's not your fault.

00:42:16.300 --> 00:42:19.060
I do not have the means to stop my brethren

00:42:19.060 --> 00:42:24.530
who now tremble in the joy at the prospect of spreading their wings and flying away.

00:42:24.530 --> 00:42:28.780
We will not be bound to this place ever again.

00:42:28.780 --> 00:42:30.230
So?

00:42:30.230 --> 00:42:35.910
You will enjoy your heyday while leaving us humans behind in the twilight?

00:42:35.910 --> 00:42:39.820
Now we'll be destroyed together. What a ridiculous prospect.

00:42:40.390 --> 00:42:45.580
Some of my brethren should begin to calm down eventually.

00:42:45.580 --> 00:42:50.830
All we can do is pray that will happen in time to prevent the destruction of mankind.

00:42:51.250 --> 00:42:52.610
That's right.

00:42:52.610 --> 00:42:56.440
They've been shut-ins for a thousand years. Who knows how crazy they'll get?

00:42:56.440 --> 00:42:58.840
I'll be calmly observing the result.

00:42:59.410 --> 00:43:03.350
Child of man, you must not abandon hope.

00:43:04.730 --> 00:43:05.850
I don't know about that.

00:43:06.460 --> 00:43:09.390
Do not abandon hope.

00:43:20.180 --> 00:43:22.770
Rika! Rika!

00:43:25.620 --> 00:43:27.370
Rika!

00:43:27.370 --> 00:43:29.530
Rika, you were okay!

00:43:29.530 --> 00:43:31.520
Thank goodness!

00:43:31.520 --> 00:43:33.050
It's really a miracle!

00:43:33.050 --> 00:43:34.590
I can't believe we found you!

00:43:34.590 --> 00:43:36.000
Yeah, for sure!

00:43:36.000 --> 00:43:37.960
But we'll rejoice later.

00:43:37.960 --> 00:43:40.360
For now, we have to escape.

00:43:40.360 --> 00:43:41.740
That's right.

00:43:41.740 --> 00:43:42.050
Come on!

00:43:46.180 --> 00:43:48.710
Rika, what's wrong?

00:43:48.710 --> 00:43:50.390
We have to get out of here.

00:43:52.650 --> 00:43:54.730
What's going on, Rika-chan?

00:43:54.730 --> 00:43:58.050
If we stay here, we don't know what'll happen!

00:43:58.050 --> 00:44:00.030
That's right. We have to escape.

00:44:01.170 --> 00:44:03.490
I will stay here.

00:44:05.580 --> 00:44:11.550
If <i>we</i> don't stay here, no one will remember that this is where <i>we're</i> supposed to be.

00:44:11.550 --> 00:44:15.420
So, I'm sorry, but I can't leave.

00:44:15.420 --> 00:44:19.890
It'll be okay. Soon, it won't be dangerous here anymore.

00:44:19.890 --> 00:44:23.680
Everyone will kill each other and no one will be left alive.

00:44:23.680 --> 00:44:26.680
What are you saying? We have to leave now!

00:44:26.680 --> 00:44:30.520
I told you, didn't I? I cannot leave this place.

00:44:31.780 --> 00:44:34.020
I have to observe this.

00:44:34.020 --> 00:44:40.020
Is it the end of the world, or the beginning of a new one?

00:44:40.020 --> 00:44:42.450
As the reincarnation of Oyashiro-sama, I must.

00:44:43.000 --> 00:44:44.030
Rika.

00:44:44.030 --> 00:44:48.210
But... let's... let's go together!

00:44:48.210 --> 00:44:49.080
Rika-chan.

00:44:49.700 --> 00:44:51.980
This is what I must do.

00:44:51.980 --> 00:44:55.450
So, in my place, please watch over the world.

00:44:55.450 --> 00:45:02.090
And see whether we can accept new friends or not.

00:45:02.090 --> 00:45:04.340
New... friends?

00:45:04.340 --> 00:45:07.770
I'll be waiting here until then.

00:45:07.770 --> 00:45:11.350
Until someone returns, I will wait.

00:45:12.630 --> 00:45:14.250
Rika...

00:45:14.250 --> 00:45:17.610
Is that what you truly must do?

00:45:19.940 --> 00:45:21.170
Rika!

00:45:25.370 --> 00:45:27.050
Okay, Rika-chan.

00:45:27.780 --> 00:45:32.490
I... no, <i>we</i> will definitely come back!

00:45:32.490 --> 00:45:36.120
So promise me you won't die until then!

00:45:36.120 --> 00:45:38.160
I promise.

00:45:38.160 --> 00:45:39.630
We will meet again.

00:45:40.020 --> 00:45:41.660
Then there's nothing to worry about.

00:45:41.660 --> 00:45:46.660
Satoko, the reincarnation of
Oyashiro-sama promised you.

00:45:46.660 --> 00:45:48.950
You'll definitely see her again!

00:45:51.290 --> 00:45:54.140
Rika-chan, you better keep your promise.

00:45:56.730 --> 00:45:59.430
Till then, take care of yourself.

00:46:01.190 --> 00:46:02.350
Bye.

00:46:07.400 --> 00:46:10.940
You better! Rika!

00:46:13.950 --> 00:46:18.740
Fight on! Nano desu~!

00:46:27.060 --> 00:46:30.510
It looks like it's spread this far already.

00:46:30.510 --> 00:46:33.030
Is this the end of the world?

00:46:33.030 --> 00:46:34.470
I don't know.

00:46:34.470 --> 00:46:39.190
But Rika-chan knows this is probably a new beginning.

00:46:39.190 --> 00:46:42.440
Through the artifice known as civilization,

00:46:42.440 --> 00:46:48.410
humanity spent a thousand years thinking it was the only exception to natural selection.

00:46:48.950 --> 00:46:53.030
And now we're paying the bill for all that borrowed time.

00:46:53.650 --> 00:46:58.670
Is this mad world going to be
our normal one from now on?

00:46:59.410 --> 00:47:01.980
This "mad world" will end soon.

00:47:01.980 --> 00:47:06.580
Only those who accept the new
world will survive. Natural selection.

00:47:07.320 --> 00:47:13.930
Well, it remains to be seen if we'll pass that selection.

00:47:13.930 --> 00:47:15.460
Oh come on.

00:47:15.460 --> 00:47:19.020
We can get through this no problem.

00:47:19.020 --> 00:47:22.690
It's nothing compared to the
usual trouble we face in our club.

00:47:22.690 --> 00:47:26.360
Living by the new rules in this world...

00:47:26.360 --> 00:47:32.450
Well, it looks like our next club activities will be rather heavy and last for quite a while.

00:47:32.970 --> 00:47:34.910
Living in an unfair world?

00:47:34.910 --> 00:47:38.710
That means the rules of the game haven't really changed at all.

00:47:38.710 --> 00:47:40.500
That's true too.

00:47:40.500 --> 00:47:41.710
Yup!

00:47:41.710 --> 00:47:43.730
The real test starts now.

00:47:43.730 --> 00:47:49.720
The Great Hinamizawa Disaster, but on a global scale, will finally begin.

00:47:49.720 --> 00:47:52.470
Everyone, let's all brace ourselves!

00:47:52.760 --> 00:47:54.190
Yeah!

00:48:11.880 --> 00:48:17.840
Where are you now and what are you doing?

00:48:17.840 --> 00:48:23.280
Are you in that place beyond the sky?

00:48:40.940 --> 00:48:46.820
When I lost the things that have filled my heart till now

00:48:46.820 --> 00:48:52.530
I realized for the first time

00:48:52.530 --> 00:48:58.320
how much you supported me

00:48:58.320 --> 00:49:03.730
and how much you made me smile

00:49:03.730 --> 00:49:15.550
The cost of losing them was unbearable

00:49:15.550 --> 00:49:21.140
Even though I struggled so desperately

00:49:21.330 --> 00:49:26.840
to reach out my hands and take them back

00:49:26.840 --> 00:49:32.830
Like the wind they slipped through,

00:49:32.830 --> 00:49:38.780
looking as though they would reach me, but did not

00:49:38.780 --> 00:49:44.550
My chest tightened with loneliness and despair

00:49:44.550 --> 00:49:50.260
My heart felt like it would break

00:49:50.330 --> 00:49:56.200
But your smiling face remained in my memories

00:49:56.200 --> 00:50:02.600
and always encourages me

00:50:24.790 --> 00:50:30.510
Let's return to those days once more

00:50:30.510 --> 00:50:36.290
I know it will be all right this time

00:50:36.640 --> 00:50:42.040
I'll always be by your side, smiling

00:50:42.040 --> 00:50:48.180
Right by your side...

00:50:48.180 --> 00:50:54.040
Where are you now and what are you doing?

00:50:54.040 --> 00:50:59.640
Are you in that place beyond the sky?

00:50:59.640 --> 00:51:05.460
Will you be there for me, smiling like always?

00:51:05.460 --> 00:51:11.880
Right now, that's all I keep hoping for

00:51:43.230 --> 00:51:49.240
Where are you now and what are you doing?

00:51:49.240 --> 00:51:57.180
Are you in that place beyond the sky?
